00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:36.570
And I said, well, she was, I kind of tried to describe her, I was like, as I was describing
我说，嗯，她……我试着描述她的样子，我说着说着，

317
00:13:36.570 --> 00:13:43.550
her, I realized, like, I was like, she's wearing a big hat and, like, a dress and sort of.
我意识到，我当时说她戴着一顶大帽子，穿着裙子之类的。

318
00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:45.770
I realized I was describing an old-timey lady.
我意识到我描述的是一位老派的女士。

319
00:13:46.570 --> 00:13:51.330
And then his face got all white, and he was like, oh, my gosh, you saw the Lavender Lady.
然后他的脸刷地一下白了，他说，天哪，你看到了“薰衣草女士”。

320
00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:52.810
What?
什么？

321
00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:53.370
Yeah.
没错。

322
00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:54.750
I'm out at that point.
那一刻我就想走人了。

323
00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:56.770
I'm, buh-bye, bye dinner theater career.
我心想，拜拜了，我的晚餐剧场生涯。

324
00:13:57.090 --> 00:13:57.570
I'm gone.
我不干了。

325
00:13:57.810 --> 00:13:59.150
I have to go entertain folks.
我还得去招待客人们。

326
00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.330
They're on their salad course.
他们正在吃沙拉呢。

327
00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:02.790
I've got to get out there and tell them a murder has happened.
我得出去告诉他们发生了一起谋杀案。

328
00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:04.070
Wow.
哇。

329
00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:04.870
Yeah.
是啊。

330
00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:07.510
Oh, my gosh, that's creepy.
天哪，那太诡异了。

331
00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:08.170
Yeah.
确实。

332
00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:10.530
Wow, you did dinner theater, lady.
哇，你居然做过晚餐剧场，女士。

333
00:14:10.690 --> 00:14:13.530
You did theater while someone was, like, buttering a baguette.
你居然在别人抹法棍面包的时候表演戏剧。

334
00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:14.730
Well, here's the thing.
嗯，情况是这样的。

335
00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:16.010
We did it between courses.
我们是在上菜间隙表演的。

336
00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:17.530
So we'd bring everybody in.
所以我们会把大家带进来。

337
00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:18.450
We'd sit them down.
让他们坐下。

338
00:14:18.570 --> 00:14:19.490
They're getting their drinks.
他们正在喝饮料。

339
00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:20.890
We're handing out slips of paper.
我们则在分发纸条。

340
00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:26.890
It was our job during this mingle to find the people who seemed outgoing enough to play
我们在这种社交环节的工作，就是找出那些看起来足够外向的人，让他们扮演

341
00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:27.910
the major roles.
主要角色。

342
00:14:28.110 --> 00:14:29.570
Because you don't want to give.
因为你肯定不想把角色给……

343
00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:30.090
Wait, wait.
等等，等等。

344
00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:32.130
The people eating dinner play a part?
吃晚餐的人也要参与表演？

345
00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:32.770
Oh, yes.
哦，是的。

346
00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:34.170
Everybody gets a part.
每个人都有角色。

347
00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:36.030
Everybody has a funny name.
每个人都有个滑稽的名字。

348
00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:38.270
Someone in the room is the murderer.
房间里的某个人就是凶手。

349
00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:40.090
Oh, I didn't realize that.
哦，我之前没意识到这一点。

350
00:14:40.170 --> 00:14:45.110
I thought you were performing a murder mystery while people ate dinner and watched you.
我还以为你们是在人们吃晚餐看戏的时候表演谋杀悬疑剧呢。

351
00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:45.490
No.
不。

352
00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:49.730
Interactive, improvisation-slash-scripted.
互动式的，即兴加剧本的。

353
00:14:49.730 --> 00:14:50.910
We had jokes.
我们有笑话。

354
00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:53.650
We had to keep people kind of on the plot.
我们得让大家大致跟着剧情走。

355
00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:57.190
But, you know, you'd walk people to their table.
但你知道，你会领着客人去他们的桌子。

356
00:14:57.930 --> 00:14:59.110
Waiters giving them a drink.
服务员给他们送上饮料。

357
00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:00.750
You're hobnobbing with them in character.
你得在角色中与他们寒暄。

358
00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:04.390
And you find the people that seem like they can play the different roles.
然后你会找出那些看起来能扮演不同角色的人。

359
00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:06.930
And then you've got these slips of paper and you hand it to them.
接着你手里拿着这些小纸条，递给他们。

360
00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:11.050
And then later you'd be like, where's Bobby Oylton?
后来你就会问，Bobby Oylton在哪儿？

361
00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:12.450
Bobby Oylton?
Bobby Oylton？

362
00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:13.070
Oh, yes.
哦，是的。

363
00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:14.950
I saw you when you came in.
你进来的时候我就看见你了。

364
00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:17.930
Bobby, what do you have to say for yourself?
Bobby，你有什么要为自己辩解的吗？

365
00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:21.090
And then he has to read off of his little slip of paper.
然后他就得照着他的小纸条念。

366
00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:22.570
You were Michael Scott.
你当时是Michael Scott。

367
00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:24.310
Yes, I sort of was.
是的，算是吧。

368
00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:25.450
You were Caleb Crawdad.
你当时是Caleb Crawdad。

369
00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:27.570
I was sort of Caleb Crawdad, yeah.
我算是Caleb Crawdad，没错。

370
00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:28.710
Wow.
哇。

371
00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:29.550
Yeah.
是啊。

372
00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:32.210
So I did that for two years.
所以我干了两年。

373
00:15:32.770 --> 00:15:34.910
But I got 50 bucks a night.
但我一晚能拿50块钱。

374
00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:37.010
That was, like, good money.
那算是不错的收入了。

375
00:15:37.670 --> 00:15:38.630
For acting.
演戏的话。

376
00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:39.930
For doing what I loved.
做我热爱的事。

377
00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:44.350
I need mom detectives to go to a murder mystery dinner theater.
我需要妈妈侦探们去参加一场谋杀之谜晚餐剧场。

378
00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:46.430
Put it on a card, Jenna.
记在卡片上，Jenna。

379
00:15:46.430 --> 00:15:49.850
Yeah, we should investigate the Lavender Lady sighting.
对，我们应该调查一下薰衣草夫人的目击事件。

380
00:15:50.070 --> 00:15:50.510
Yes.
没错。

381
00:15:51.070 --> 00:15:52.510
We'll get to the bottom of it.
我们会查个水落石出。

382
00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:55.110
We will, but we'll have to be in character and wear outfits.
我们会查清楚的，但我们得进入角色并穿上戏服。

383
00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:58.290
Yes, because we'll pretend like we're part of the dinner theater.
对，因为我们要假装自己是晚餐剧场的一部分。

384
00:15:58.290 --> 00:15:58.890
We're part of the show.
我们是演出的一部分。

385
00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:00.790
My God, it writes itself.
天哪，这剧本简直是现成的。

386
00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:02.650
My God.
天哪。

387
00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:06.550
If I see this on TV one day, I'm going to be so pissed.
如果有一天我在电视上看到这个，我会非常火大。

388
00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:08.570
I'm going to kick someone's ass if it's not you and I.
如果不是你和我演的，我非得踢某人的屁股不可。

389
00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:09.590
I know.
我知道。

390
00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:10.570
Kicking some butts.
踢屁股。

391
00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:13.350
All right, let's take a break and call our agents.
好了，休息一下，给我们的经纪人打电话吧。

392
00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:24.780
We are back.
我们回来了。

393
00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:31.980
And today only, Dwight Schrute presents This Year in Martial Arts, colon updates, advancements,
仅限今天，Dwight Schrute为您呈现《年度武术》，冒号，更新、进展，

394
00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:32.660
and et cetera.
等等。

395
00:16:32.940 --> 00:16:39.840
Yes, like Jim said, there's always lots of changes to the 1,000-year-old martial arts traditions.
是的，正如Jim所说，有着千年历史的武术传统总是有很多变化。

396
00:16:40.740 --> 00:16:42.360
Dwight's going to start with Phyllis.
Dwight要从Phyllis开始讲起。

397
00:16:42.700 --> 00:16:43.900
I clocked some moves.
我记录了一些动作。

398
00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:47.460
Phyllis charges Dwight with what looks to be a two-finger eye jab.
Phyllis向Dwight发起了攻击，看起来像是双指戳眼。

399
00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:48.040
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

400
00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:51.600
Dwight stops her with an arm block that I guess would have broken her arm, and then he's
Dwight用手臂格挡住了她，我猜这本该折断她的手臂，然后他

401
00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:52.460
going to flip her over.
准备把她翻过来。

402
00:16:53.020 --> 00:16:55.400
Yeah, he tries to engage Kevin.
没错，他试图和凯文互动。

403
00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:56.480
Kevin's a big no.
凯文完全不买账。

404
00:16:56.860 --> 00:16:57.300
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

405
00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:00.700
And all of this is going to lead to Dwight fighting himself.
而这一切最终会导致德怀特自己跟自己打架。

406
00:17:01.440 --> 00:17:01.840
Yes.
是的。

407
00:17:02.780 --> 00:17:07.740
I'd like to point out in this scene at 39 seconds, Meredith is wearing the designer sweater
我想指出的是，在这一幕的39秒处，梅雷迪斯又穿上了那件设计师款毛衣

408
00:17:07.740 --> 00:17:08.340
vest again.
背心。

409
00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:10.020
I clocked that, too.
我也注意到了。

410
00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:13.320
I mean, I feel like this is some sort of personal trolling of me.
我的意思是，我觉得这简直是在针对我个人。

411
00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:16.860
Well, I have a few tidbits about this cold open.
好吧，关于这段开场戏，我有一些小花絮。

412
00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:17.920
Oh, really?
哦，真的吗？

413
00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:19.220
I have some as well.
我也有一些。

414
00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:25.920
Well, I'll start by saying we got a lot of mail of people asking if Dwight's self-fight
那我就先说，我们收到了很多邮件，人们都在问德怀特的自我对打

415
00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:30.880
was choreographed, and I would like to tell you guys that was all Rainn Wilson.
是不是编排好的，我想告诉大家，那全都是雷恩·威尔逊自己完成的。

416
00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:32.640
Bravo, Rainn!
太棒了，雷恩！

417
00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:33.100
Yes.
没错。

418
00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:37.340
He came up with all of those moves based on descriptions in the script.
他根据剧本里的描述，想出了所有的动作。

419
00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:42.720
We did have our stunt coordinator, Eric Sulke, on board for the day just to make sure that
我们确实请了特技协调员埃里克·苏尔克在现场待了一天，以确保

420
00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:44.340
Rainn didn't actually hurt himself.
雷恩不会真的伤到自己。

421
00:17:44.340 --> 00:17:49.780
Well, in the DVD commentary, Danny shared that the original version of this cold open
在DVD评论音轨里，丹尼分享说这段开场戏的原始版本

422
00:17:49.780 --> 00:17:53.900
ended with Dwight and Michael kicking each other in the groin.
结尾是德怀特和迈克尔互相踢对方的裆部。

423
00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:54.700
Oh.
哦。

424
00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:55.440
Yeah.
是啊。

425
00:17:55.740 --> 00:18:01.860
But instead, they went with a pitch from Jen Salata where Dwight fights himself instead.
但后来他们采纳了简·萨拉塔的提议，改成了德怀特自己跟自己打架。

426
00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:08.640
It still ends with Dwight punching himself in the groin, but it was originally scripted to
虽然结尾还是德怀特自己给了自己裆部一拳，但最初剧本里写的是

427
00:18:08.640 --> 00:18:11.780
be a self-kick in the groin.
自己踢自己的裆部。

428
00:18:12.140 --> 00:18:13.240
It said this.
剧本是这么写的。

429
00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:14.800
How do you kick yourself in the groin?
人怎么可能踢到自己的裆部？

430
00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:16.080
Exactly.
就是说啊。

431
00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:16.540
Yeah.
没错。

432
00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:18.560
Here's what the script said.
剧本上是这么写的。

433
00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:19.260
Quote,
引用如下：

434
00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:23.120
Dwight snaps his leg up and kicks himself in the balls.
德怀特猛地抬起腿，踢向自己的蛋蛋。

435
00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:28.600
Dwight's face shows equally the pain of the kick and the pride of winning.
德怀特的脸上既表现出被踢的痛苦，又表现出获胜的自豪。

436
00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:30.680
That's so great.
太搞笑了。

437
00:18:31.760 --> 00:18:37.860
On the day, they realized there was no way for Rainn to self-kick himself in the balls,
拍摄当天，他们意识到雷恩根本没法自己踢到自己的蛋蛋，

438
00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:40.180
that it was just sort of physically impossible.
这在物理上几乎是不可能的。

439
00:18:40.460 --> 00:18:48.060
However, Danny said in an interview that Greg was convinced there was a way to do it.
不过，丹尼在采访中说，格雷格坚信一定有办法做到。

440
00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:57.320
If maybe they could attach a strap to Rainn's leg that would help sort of hoist it up somehow.
比如他们能不能在雷恩的腿上绑根带子，帮他把腿吊起来之类的。

441
00:18:57.640 --> 00:19:03.520
He even sketched it out on the back of his script, which is a very Greg move.
他甚至在剧本背面画了草图，这非常符合格雷格的风格。

442
00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:08.620
Can't you see Greg turning his script over and like sketching out the self-groin kick strap?
你能想象格雷格翻过剧本，画出那个自我踢裆装置的样子吗？

443
00:19:08.980 --> 00:19:09.960
Here's how it works.
它是这样运作的。

444
00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:10.760
Here's the mechanics.
原理是这样的。

445
00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.160
I want that sketch and I want it in a frame.
我想要那张草图，还要把它装裱起来。

446
00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:13.640
Right?
对吧？

447
00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:14.880
Where is that sketch?
那张草图在哪儿呢？

448
00:19:15.600 --> 00:19:21.360
In the end, obviously, this was not happening, so they had Rainn punch himself in the groin.
最后，显然这没法实现，所以他们让雷恩自己给了自己裆部一拳。

449
00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:26.360
Greg shared that he really enjoyed directing the cold open and the tag for this episode
格雷格分享说，他非常喜欢执导这一集的开场戏和结尾彩蛋，

450
00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:32.860
because they were like mini action movies or the closest thing our show got to little action sequences.
因为它们就像迷你动作片，或者说是我们剧集里最接近动作场面的东西了。

451
00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:34.780
And Jenna, Ellie shared something.
还有珍娜，艾莉分享了一件事。

452
00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:38.860
She said the cold open was filmed the morning of the Emmys.
她说开场戏是在艾美奖颁奖礼那天早上拍的。

453
00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:44.020
Oh, so after Rainn beat himself up, he had to go to the Emmys?
噢，所以雷恩在把自己打了一顿之后，还得去参加艾美奖？

454
00:19:44.020 --> 00:19:45.120
We all did.
我们都去了。

455
00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:46.320
Wow.
哇。

456
00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:47.360
We worked that day.
我们那天还要工作。

457
00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:54.960
We have shared this before that many times we worked right up until an event and we would have to get ready at the set.
我们之前分享过，很多时候我们工作到活动开始前一刻，还得在片场准备。

458
00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:55.620
Yeah.
是啊。

459
00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.600
And the Emmys were traditionally on a Monday night.
而且艾美奖传统上是在周一晚上举行。

460
00:19:58.860 --> 00:19:59.220
Yeah.
没错。

461
00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:03.420
Which was rough because it would be like the beginning of your work week.
那挺难熬的，因为那就像是你工作周的开始。

462
00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:06.400
Oh, and you'd be wrecked for the whole rest of the week.
噢，那你接下来的一整周都会累垮的。

463
00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:07.480
Wow.
哇。

464
00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:10.180
We worked this day and then we went to the Emmys.
我们那天工作完就直接去参加艾美奖了。

465
00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:12.360
Oh, one last thing.
噢，最后还有一件事。

466
00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:14.840
I have a Dwight flyer count.
我统计了一下德怀特的传单数量。

467
00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:15.640
Oh.
噢。

468
00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:20.300
Because clearly you need to have multiple flyers for your year-end martial art update.
因为显然你的年终武术更新需要多张传单。

469
00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:20.920
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

470
00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:26.780
We have one on each of Jim's glass walls and we have one on the door by accounting.
吉姆的每块玻璃墙上各有一张，会计部旁边的门上也有一张。

471
00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:29.560
Three in view during the whole cold open.
整个开场戏里能看到三张。

472
00:20:29.780 --> 00:20:31.120
I don't know about the rest of the bullpen.
不知道办公区其他地方还有没有。

473
00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:32.340
Or the kitchen.
或者厨房里。

474
00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:33.320
Or the break room.
或者休息室里。

475
00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:33.900
I know.
我知道。

476
00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:35.020
I'm sure they're everywhere.
我肯定到处都是。

477
00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:39.340
They're not there for the rest of the episode, but there's three visible for the cold open.
这集剩下的部分里它们就不在了，但在开场戏里能看到三张。

478
00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:41.500
Well, now we're going to get into this episode.
好了，现在我们要进入这一集的内容了。

479
00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:48.740
It opens with some weird banter between Michael and Andy about sculpting stand-up comedy.
开场是迈克尔和安迪之间关于雕塑脱口秀的一些奇怪调侃。

480
00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:52.820
And it's interrupted by Dwight receiving an email.
然后被德怀特收到的一封邮件打断了。

481
00:20:53.160 --> 00:20:55.380
And Michael's like, you need to be more specific.
迈克尔说，你需要说得更具体一点。

482
00:20:55.380 --> 00:20:57.260
I get like eight emails a day.
我一天大概收到八封邮件。

483
00:20:57.500 --> 00:20:58.120
Eight, Jenna.
八封，珍娜。

484
00:20:58.420 --> 00:20:59.620
He gets eight.
他只收到八封。

485
00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:05.760
It's really weird that before we started recording today, we were discussing our email inboxes.
真奇怪，今天录制开始前，我们还在讨论各自的收件箱。

486
00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:06.700
Yeah.
是啊。

487
00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:10.480
So, guys, Sam and Jenna are really tidy about their email inbox.
所以，伙计们，萨姆和珍娜对她们的收件箱管理得非常整洁。

488
00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:18.160
Like, they get to zero and then they ask me what my inbox said and my inbox says 1,582.
比如，她们会清理到零封，然后问我的收件箱有多少，我的收件箱显示有1582封。

489
00:21:18.680 --> 00:21:24.580
And Sam and I are still processing that and we're – it gave you like hives for a minute.
萨姆和我还在消化这件事，我们——这让你难受了一会儿。

490
00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:25.900
Yeah, we're having a hard time.
是啊，我们很难接受。

491
00:21:25.900 --> 00:21:29.540
I don't mean this as an attack, but the way you live is chaos.
我不是想攻击你，但你的生活方式简直是一团糟。

492
00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:34.240
Sam's at zero right now.
萨姆现在是零封。

493
00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:36.560
I'm at 10 unread emails.
我有10封未读邮件。

494
00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:42.040
Actually, do you remember in the break, there was a great Jenna moment where you were looking for an email and you couldn't find it.
对了，你还记得休息的时候吗，有个很棒的珍娜时刻，你在找一封邮件却找不到。

495
00:21:42.100 --> 00:21:43.660
And Jenna goes, oh, I'm sorry, can you not?
然后珍娜说，噢，抱歉，你能别这样吗？

496
00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:44.520
Yeah.
是啊。

497
00:21:44.660 --> 00:21:47.100
I was like, oh, you can't find the email I sent you?
我当时想，噢，你找不到我发给你的邮件？

498
00:21:47.840 --> 00:21:50.020
I think I sent it on Monday or Tuesday.
我想我是周一或周二发的。

499
00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:55.600
Well, I got a few emails since I last checked and now I'm 1,583.
好吧，我上次查看之后又收到了几封，现在我有1583封了。

500
00:21:56.280 --> 00:22:06.600
See, you do what Lee does, which is if you can tell that it's something you don't need to read, like it's, I don't know, an ad or something, you don't delete it.
看吧，你和李一样，如果看出是不需要读的内容，比如广告之类的，你就不去删它。

501
00:22:06.700 --> 00:22:07.560
You just skip it.
你直接跳过就行了。

502
00:22:07.740 --> 00:22:09.360
And then it stays unread.
然后它就一直显示未读。

503
00:22:09.540 --> 00:22:09.880
Yes.
没错。

504
00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:11.320
I delete those.
我会把那些删掉。

505
00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:13.260
I don't want that cluttering me.
我不想让它们弄乱我的收件箱。

506
00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:14.580
No, you do it right.
不，你得用正确的方法。

507
00:22:14.920 --> 00:22:16.420
That's the way you should do it.
那才是你应该做的方式。

508
00:22:16.420 --> 00:22:18.940
But if it doesn't bother you, then you're not doing it wrong.
但如果它没困扰到你，那你也没做错。

509
00:22:18.940 --> 00:22:21.060
It would bother me if I did it your way.
如果我按你的方式做，我会被困扰到。

510
00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:25.600
Well, Michael only gets eight, so I guess he's not super stressed out.
好吧，迈克尔只有八封邮件，所以我猜他压力没那么大。

511
00:22:26.040 --> 00:22:27.240
I guess he's not.
我想也是。

512
00:22:28.120 --> 00:22:34.620
The email that Dwight is talking about is from David Wallace and it is referring to an article in the journal.
德怀特提到的那封邮件来自大卫·华莱士，它指的是期刊上的一篇文章。

513
00:22:35.220 --> 00:22:36.420
I mean, the wall.
我是说，那堵墙。

514
00:22:36.820 --> 00:22:37.300
Yeah.
对。

515
00:22:37.300 --> 00:22:38.760
As Michael calls it.
正如迈克尔所称呼的那样。

516
00:22:38.980 --> 00:22:40.100
Oh, the wall, right?
哦，那堵墙，对吧？

517
00:22:40.900 --> 00:22:47.420
Oscar finds the article, but in order to read it, you have to pay an extra $1.99 to get past the paywall.
奥斯卡找到了那篇文章，但为了阅读它，你必须额外支付1.99美元才能绕过付费墙。

518
00:22:48.100 --> 00:22:55.100
Danny shared that they spent like five hours researching the rules of the Wall Street Journal's paywall at that time.
丹尼分享说，他们当时花了大约五个小时研究《华尔街日报》付费墙的规则。

519
00:22:55.300 --> 00:23:02.060
He said, apparently, if you're referencing a specific publication, you cannot make up a fact like that that's not true.
他说，显然，如果你引用特定的出版物，你就不能编造那种不属实的事实。

520
00:23:02.060 --> 00:23:06.040
Oh, so at that time, that was the rule.
哦，所以当时那是规则。

521
00:23:06.220 --> 00:23:07.080
Of the paywall.
关于付费墙的。

522
00:23:07.520 --> 00:23:07.980
Interesting.
有意思。

523
00:23:08.300 --> 00:23:10.740
Why did it take five hours to get that information?
为什么获取那个信息要花五个小时？

524
00:23:11.120 --> 00:23:12.880
I think they just had to get it correctly.
我想他们只是必须确保准确无误。

525
00:23:13.080 --> 00:23:15.360
And Jenna, they didn't have the Google back then.
而且珍娜，那时候他们还没有谷歌。

526
00:23:15.640 --> 00:23:17.740
They had Google back then.
那时候他们有谷歌。

527
00:23:17.740 --> 00:23:19.440
It was like 2009.
那是2009年左右。

528
00:23:20.100 --> 00:23:22.200
They didn't have the same search engines we had.
他们当时没有我们现在用的这种搜索引擎。

529
00:23:22.260 --> 00:23:23.140
Yeah, 100% they did.
不，他们绝对有。

530
00:23:24.580 --> 00:23:27.180
How old do you think Google is?
你觉得谷歌有多老了？

531
00:23:27.520 --> 00:23:28.380
It's new.
它很新。

532
00:23:28.680 --> 00:23:29.700
Google is new.
谷歌很新。

533
00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:32.420
I'm going to Google, when did Google start?
我要去搜一下，谷歌是什么时候开始的？

534
00:23:32.820 --> 00:23:37.620
Well, I don't know why it took them five hours, but that's what he said on the DVD commentary.
好吧，我不知道为什么他们花了五个小时，但那是他在DVD评论音轨里说的。

535
00:23:37.900 --> 00:23:39.520
They had to be thorough, Jenna.
他们必须做到详尽，珍娜。

536
00:23:40.220 --> 00:23:42.880
What were you Googling in 2009?
你在2009年都在谷歌上搜什么？

537
00:23:43.380 --> 00:23:44.600
Don't put this on us.
别把这事推到我们头上。

538
00:23:44.760 --> 00:23:45.180
Any number.
随便哪个数字。

539
00:23:45.680 --> 00:23:46.760
I'm not saying you.
我不是说你。

540
00:23:46.880 --> 00:23:49.160
I'm saying people listening.
我是说听众们。

541
00:23:49.940 --> 00:23:50.660
Hold on.
等等。

542
00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:52.680
What did you Google in 2009?
你在2009年搜过什么？

543
00:23:53.080 --> 00:23:56.260
Google started September 4th, 1998.
谷歌始于1998年9月4日。

544
00:23:56.820 --> 00:23:58.300
But their search engine.
但他们的搜索引擎。

545
00:23:58.300 --> 00:24:00.060
That's, I'm going to get more specific.
那个，我要说得更具体一点。

546
00:24:00.440 --> 00:24:00.520
Thank you.
谢谢。

547
00:24:01.180 --> 00:24:05.040
When did the Google search engine really come into effect?
谷歌搜索引擎到底是什么时候真正开始生效的？

548
00:24:05.280 --> 00:24:07.060
Not really come into effect.
不是真正开始生效。

549
00:24:07.320 --> 00:24:10.480
When did people start using the Google search engine?
人们是什么时候开始使用谷歌搜索引擎的？

550
00:24:11.340 --> 00:24:11.940
1998.
1998年。

551
00:24:12.460 --> 00:24:14.480
And it really became popular around 2000.
它大约在2000年左右真正流行起来。

552
00:24:14.840 --> 00:24:15.820
Thank you, Sam.
谢谢你，萨姆。

553
00:24:15.820 --> 00:24:16.880
I don't believe it.
我不敢相信。

554
00:24:17.180 --> 00:24:20.020
No one was Googling until like two years ago.
直到两年前左右，还没人会去谷歌搜索。

555
00:24:26.140 --> 00:24:29.740
Okay, everyone, Angela discovered Google a couple of years ago.
好了，各位，安吉拉是两年前才发现谷歌的。

556
00:24:29.980 --> 00:24:35.020
Listen, I don't know why it took them five hours, but they clearly had to get it right.
听着，我不知道为什么他们花了五个小时，但显然他们必须得把它弄对。

557
00:24:35.460 --> 00:24:37.040
Maybe they had to get on the phone with someone.
也许他们得跟谁通个电话。

558
00:24:37.180 --> 00:24:38.680
I'm not judging our writers, Jenna.
我没有在评判我们的编剧，珍娜。

559
00:24:38.920 --> 00:24:40.620
I just thought it was a long time.
我只是觉得时间太长了。

560
00:24:40.820 --> 00:24:42.540
Well, Jenna's judging you guys.
好吧，珍娜在评判你们。

561
00:24:42.540 --> 00:24:44.780
Here's what I want to point out about this scene.
关于这场戏，我想指出这一点。

562
00:24:44.960 --> 00:24:55.440
As we're all gathered around the computer and everybody's reading this article off of Oscar's computer, we're learning that Dunder Mifflin might be, I guess, going into debt,
当我们都围在电脑旁，每个人都在读奥斯卡电脑上的这篇文章时，我们了解到邓德·米夫林公司可能，我想，要负债了，

563
00:24:55.600 --> 00:24:57.340
going under, filing for bankruptcy.
要倒闭了，要申请破产了。

564
00:24:57.540 --> 00:24:57.680
Yeah.
没错。

565
00:24:58.420 --> 00:25:02.720
Angela, this entire scene, you are blocking me.
安吉拉，整场戏你都在挡着我。

566
00:25:03.160 --> 00:25:07.460
You cannot see my face in this scene because you are standing directly in front of me.
在这场戏里你根本看不到我的脸，因为你就站在我正前方。

567
00:25:07.600 --> 00:25:12.080
And then finally, you move out of the way and John blocks me.
最后你终于让开了，结果约翰又挡住了我。

568
00:25:12.420 --> 00:25:13.580
Did you take a picture?
你拍照了吗？

569
00:25:13.940 --> 00:25:14.640
Yes, I did.
拍了。

570
00:25:14.660 --> 00:25:19.100
It was so funny to me because one of you is blocking me the whole time.
我觉得太搞笑了，因为你们俩全程有一个人在挡着我。

571
00:25:19.300 --> 00:25:23.180
We talked that morning and we were like, today is the day, John.
那天早上我们聊过，当时我们说，就是今天了，约翰。

572
00:25:23.180 --> 00:25:29.400
John, you and I, I'm going to wear my three-inch heels and I'm going to make sure I block that shot.
约翰，你和我，我要穿上我的三英寸高跟鞋，确保我能挡住那个镜头。

573
00:25:29.560 --> 00:25:31.120
Here, I put them all together.
给你，我把它们都拼在一起了。

574
00:25:31.840 --> 00:25:33.040
We really are.
我们确实是。

575
00:25:33.460 --> 00:25:35.080
Why didn't anyone say anything?
为什么没人说点什么？

576
00:25:35.300 --> 00:25:36.060
I don't know.
我不知道。

577
00:25:36.700 --> 00:25:41.340
So we don't know how Pam feels about this article because we can never see her.
所以我们不知道帕姆对这篇文章有什么感想，因为我们根本看不到她。

578
00:25:41.520 --> 00:25:41.800
You can't see her face.
你看不见她的脸。

579
00:25:42.660 --> 00:25:43.180
Sorry.
抱歉。

580
00:25:46.200 --> 00:25:48.680
I rarely was able to block anyone.
我很少能挡住别人。

581
00:25:49.240 --> 00:25:50.660
Personal victory, I guess.
我想这算是个人的胜利吧。

582
00:25:50.800 --> 00:25:51.180
I know.
我知道。

583
00:25:51.760 --> 00:25:54.680
Well, what's funny is they all stop at the $1.99.
有趣的是，他们都停在了1.99美元那里。

584
00:25:54.920 --> 00:25:58.060
They're like, oh, I guess we're not going to know what really happens with the company.
他们就像是，哦，看来我们没法知道公司到底会发生什么了。

585
00:25:58.280 --> 00:25:59.920
And then Jim enters in his information.
然后吉姆输入了他的信息。

586
00:26:00.540 --> 00:26:00.780
Yes.
是的。

587
00:26:00.980 --> 00:26:04.820
This sends Michael on a spiral and he calls David Wallace.
这让迈克尔陷入了混乱，他给大卫·华莱士打了电话。

588
00:26:05.100 --> 00:26:06.340
But David's in a meeting.
但大卫正在开会。

589
00:26:07.100 --> 00:26:09.860
I was curious about two moments in this scene.
我对这场戏里的两个时刻很好奇。

590
00:26:10.260 --> 00:26:10.720
Okay.
好的。

591
00:26:11.200 --> 00:26:14.940
One was I was wondering if Steve improvised the way he said,
一个是我想知道史蒂夫说那句台词的方式是不是即兴发挥的，

592
00:26:15.140 --> 00:26:16.480
you should spy on him.
你应该监视他。

593
00:26:16.620 --> 00:26:18.100
Wouldn't that be so hilarious?
那难道不是很搞笑吗？

594
00:26:19.020 --> 00:26:19.500
Okay.
好的。

595
00:26:20.280 --> 00:26:22.820
I was like, did they tell Steve to say it like that?
我在想，是不是有人告诉史蒂夫要那样说？

596
00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:28.220
I went to the script and it said on that line, in parentheses, Valley Girl.
我查了剧本，那句台词的括号里写着：山谷女孩腔。

597
00:26:28.560 --> 00:26:29.540
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

598
00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:33.060
So they did give him sort of a line read.
所以他们确实给了他某种台词指导。

599
00:26:33.060 --> 00:26:33.620
Yes.
是的。

600
00:26:34.020 --> 00:26:37.760
The other thing I was curious about was the line in the script when Michael says,
我好奇的另一件事是剧本里迈克尔说的那句台词，

601
00:26:37.900 --> 00:26:39.040
catch you on the flippity flip.
回头再聊。

602
00:26:39.300 --> 00:26:39.820
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

603
00:26:39.900 --> 00:26:41.960
I was like, that sounds like something Steve would improvise.
我当时就想，这听起来像是史蒂夫会即兴发挥出来的台词。

604
00:26:42.360 --> 00:26:42.800
No.
不是。

605
00:26:43.060 --> 00:26:45.180
So that line was in the script, too.
所以那句台词也是剧本里写的。

606
00:26:45.340 --> 00:26:50.420
And Danny shared on the DVD commentary that Gene Stepnitsky actually pitched,
丹尼在DVD评论音轨里分享说，其实是吉恩·斯特普尼茨基提议的，

607
00:26:50.620 --> 00:26:53.480
catch you on the flippity flip, for a different episode.
“回头再聊”，原本是为另一集准备的。

608
00:26:53.480 --> 00:26:56.240
And the writers loved it, but it didn't make it in.
编剧们很喜欢，但那一集没用上。

609
00:26:56.240 --> 00:26:58.140
And so they kept trying to get this line in.
所以他们一直想把这句台词加进去。

610
00:26:58.280 --> 00:26:59.140
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

611
00:26:59.480 --> 00:27:00.200
Episode after episode.
一集又一集。

612
00:27:00.440 --> 00:27:01.660
And they finally got it in.
最后他们终于把它加进去了。

613
00:27:01.960 --> 00:27:04.500
Well, you know when Michael goes to the bathroom and he's been vomiting,
你知道迈克尔去洗手间呕吐那段吗？

614
00:27:04.720 --> 00:27:09.080
but then he tries to tell Kevin he was just pooping.
但他后来试图告诉凯文他只是在拉屎。

615
00:27:09.420 --> 00:27:11.900
We had a fan question from Kelly C in Michigan.
我们收到了一位来自密歇根州的粉丝凯莉·C的提问。

616
00:27:11.980 --> 00:27:14.800
Who wrote the line, just pooping, you know how I be?
是谁写了“只是拉屎，你知道我这人就这样”这句台词？

617
00:27:15.500 --> 00:27:16.380
That was Danny.
是丹尼。

618
00:27:17.340 --> 00:27:19.620
Danny said it's one of the lines he's most proud of.
丹尼说这是他最引以为傲的台词之一。

619
00:27:19.860 --> 00:27:21.060
It's a great line.
这台词太棒了。

620
00:27:21.060 --> 00:27:24.040
Oh, I also wanted to say one more thing, Angela.
哦，安吉拉，我还想再说一件事。

621
00:27:24.580 --> 00:27:28.220
Back in the office when Michael calls and tries to get in touch with David Wallace,
在办公室里，当迈克尔打电话试图联系大卫·华莱士时，

622
00:27:28.500 --> 00:27:32.880
once again, we had Suzanne Watson as the voice of David's assistant, Stephanie.
我们再次请到了苏珊·沃森来为大卫的助理斯蒂芬妮配音。

623
00:27:33.160 --> 00:27:34.120
And she's always great.
她一直都很棒。

624
00:27:34.340 --> 00:27:34.860
So great.
太棒了。

625
00:27:35.440 --> 00:27:41.180
So in the script, Jenna, they built in more scenes to show Michael really spiraling.
所以在剧本里，珍娜，他们增加了更多场景来表现迈克尔真的快崩溃了。

626
00:27:41.360 --> 00:27:42.720
You know, he calls David.
你知道，他给大卫打电话。

627
00:27:42.720 --> 00:27:44.080
He vomits in the bathroom.
他在洗手间呕吐。

628
00:27:44.420 --> 00:27:49.620
He also just starts pacing in front of Aaron's reception, waiting for the phone call,
他还开始在艾琳的前台前踱步，等着电话，

629
00:27:49.620 --> 00:27:52.720
waiting to see if she signals him that someone's calling.
等着看她是否会示意有人打进来了。

630
00:27:53.340 --> 00:27:54.260
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

631
00:27:54.500 --> 00:27:55.740
I want to play it for you.
我想放给你听听。

632
00:27:56.060 --> 00:27:57.060
It's in the deleted scenes.
这是删减片段里的。

633
00:27:57.220 --> 00:27:59.320
The first part I'm calling, Michael is pissed.
第一部分我打过去的时候，迈克尔气坏了。

634
00:28:00.960 --> 00:28:03.280
If it's not for me, don't make it look like it's for me, okay?
如果不是找我的，别表现得好像是找我的一样，好吗？

635
00:28:03.280 --> 00:28:03.920
I'm sorry.
对不起。

636
00:28:04.160 --> 00:28:05.680
Because I'm going to s*** my pants.
因为我快要拉裤子里了。

637
00:28:05.720 --> 00:28:06.300
Okay, I'm sorry.
好的，对不起。

638
00:28:06.480 --> 00:28:07.060
It's my fault.
是我的错。

639
00:28:13.180 --> 00:28:16.020
Michael, I'm sorry before that I did not know what you were talking about.
迈克尔，我很抱歉刚才不知道你在说什么。

640
00:28:16.580 --> 00:28:16.940
Don't.
别说了。

641
00:28:17.120 --> 00:28:17.460
Okay.
好的。

642
00:28:18.960 --> 00:28:19.660
Do you want anything for me?
你需要我为你做什么吗？

643
00:28:19.660 --> 00:28:20.300
Don't even talk.
别说话。

644
00:28:20.460 --> 00:28:21.280
Don't even talk to me.
别跟我说话。

645
00:28:21.280 --> 00:28:21.840
Okay.
好的。

646
00:28:22.600 --> 00:28:23.080
All right.
行吧。

647
00:28:23.200 --> 00:28:24.340
If they do call, don't.
如果他们真的打来，别……

648
00:28:24.440 --> 00:28:26.260
Only if they call me, then talk to me, okay?
只有他们打给我的时候，你再跟我说话，好吗？

649
00:28:26.540 --> 00:28:31.360
If it's anything else, or if you want to apologize to me for calling me when they weren't calling,
如果是其他任何事，或者你想因为刚才没电话却叫我而向我道歉，

650
00:28:32.120 --> 00:28:33.720
then don't do that, all right?
那就别做那些，好吗？

651
00:28:33.860 --> 00:28:34.480
Do you understand?
你明白吗？

652
00:28:35.780 --> 00:28:40.260
You're very, very nice, but you're really, you're kind of pissing me off, okay?
你人真的非常好，但你真的，你有点惹恼我了，好吗？

653
00:28:40.360 --> 00:28:40.520
Sorry.
抱歉。

654
00:28:40.980 --> 00:28:41.280
All right.
好吧。

655
00:28:45.040 --> 00:28:45.400
No.
不。

656
00:28:45.400 --> 00:28:46.940
Oh, I thought she lied.
噢，我以为她在撒谎。

657
00:28:47.180 --> 00:28:47.980
I thought she said sorry.
我以为她说的是抱歉。

658
00:28:48.420 --> 00:28:54.960
So her sorry looks like she's about to laugh, but then she turns it into like a cry, and
所以她的抱歉看起来像是要笑出来，但随后她又把它变成了一种哭腔，然后

659
00:28:54.960 --> 00:28:57.600
then poor Aaron, she's so confused by Michael.
可怜的艾琳，她被迈克尔搞糊涂了。

660
00:28:57.720 --> 00:28:59.320
It continues, and you've got to hear it.
还没完，你一定要听听。

661
00:29:01.200 --> 00:29:02.320
Don't cry, don't cry, please.
别哭，别哭，求你了。

662
00:29:02.680 --> 00:29:03.240
Don't cry.
别哭。

663
00:29:03.880 --> 00:29:07.260
Everybody's sort of high strung, so chalk it up to that.
大家都有点紧张，所以就把这归咎于此吧。

664
00:29:09.460 --> 00:29:10.340
We're all in it together.
我们都在同一条船上。

665
00:29:10.540 --> 00:29:11.000
Well, don't laugh either.
嗯，也别笑。

666
00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:12.280
Just don't cry and don't laugh.
就是别哭也别笑。

667
00:29:12.420 --> 00:29:12.740
Good?
行吗？

668
00:29:12.960 --> 00:29:13.300
All right.
好吧。

669
00:29:15.740 --> 00:29:17.400
It's such a funny moment.
这真是个有趣的时刻。

670
00:29:18.060 --> 00:29:19.140
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

671
00:29:19.180 --> 00:29:21.500
I love the dynamic between those two.
我喜欢他们俩之间的互动关系。

672
00:29:21.600 --> 00:29:25.380
They really did a good job of creating a different dynamic than what Pam and Michael had.
他们确实做得很好，创造出了一种与帕姆和迈克尔完全不同的互动模式。

673
00:29:25.560 --> 00:29:26.640
Yeah, I mean, Michael.
是啊，我是说，迈克尔。

674
00:29:26.640 --> 00:29:28.380
She so earnestly wants to help him.
她那么真诚地想要帮助他。

675
00:29:28.580 --> 00:29:31.360
She so earnestly wants to be liked by him.
她那么真诚地想要得到他的喜爱。

676
00:29:31.460 --> 00:29:31.680
Yeah.
是啊。

677
00:29:31.820 --> 00:29:33.680
And Michael with Pam, it's the reverse.
而迈克尔和帕姆之间，情况正好相反。

678
00:29:33.920 --> 00:29:35.680
Michael wants to be in Pam's life.
迈克尔想要进入帕姆的生活。

679
00:29:35.840 --> 00:29:36.180
Yes.
没错。

680
00:29:37.800 --> 00:29:44.320
Well, instead of all that, he's going to go into his office and play the Sean Mullins song,
嗯，他没有做那些，而是走进办公室播放了肖恩·穆林斯的歌，

681
00:29:44.500 --> 00:29:44.960
Lullaby.
《摇篮曲》。

682
00:29:45.460 --> 00:29:50.740
I found out from Randy Cordray that it cost us $45,000 to have this song in the show,
我从兰迪·科德雷那里得知，为了在剧中用这首歌，我们花了45000美元，

683
00:29:50.920 --> 00:29:51.840
to have this clip.
就是为了这段片段。

684
00:29:52.380 --> 00:29:52.760
Hmm.
嗯。

685
00:29:53.320 --> 00:29:55.160
Well, I have a background catch.
嗯，我发现了一个背景细节。

686
00:29:55.320 --> 00:30:00.760
At 5 minutes, 29 seconds, Michael says he needs more Mullins, and he hits the volume
在5分29秒时，迈克尔说他需要更多穆林斯的歌，然后他反复按下了键盘上的

687
00:30:00.760 --> 00:30:02.160
button on his keyboard repeatedly.
音量键。

688
00:30:02.440 --> 00:30:02.700
Okay.
好的。

689
00:30:02.700 --> 00:30:08.080
Greg shared that they worked really hard in editing to get that sound to match Steve hitting
格雷格分享说，他们在剪辑时非常努力，才让那个声音与史蒂夫敲击

690
00:30:08.080 --> 00:30:13.400
the keyboard, and Danny shared that after the episode aired, the comment boards were
键盘的动作对上，丹尼则分享说，剧集播出后，评论区里

691
00:30:13.400 --> 00:30:18.160
full of people saying that that was a Mac sound, and Michael is using a PC.
全是人说那是苹果电脑的声音，而迈克尔用的是个人电脑。

692
00:30:18.640 --> 00:30:20.200
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

693
00:30:20.360 --> 00:30:21.140
Isn't that funny?
这难道不好笑吗？

694
00:30:21.560 --> 00:30:22.200
Yes.
是啊。

695
00:30:22.800 --> 00:30:23.860
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

696
00:30:23.860 --> 00:30:26.640
They picked the wrong volume up sound.
他们选错了音量调节的声音。

697
00:30:27.120 --> 00:30:29.900
Well, Jim's going to come in during all of this.
嗯，吉姆会在这一切发生时走进来。

698
00:30:30.460 --> 00:30:32.780
He's like, Michael, you have to pull it together.
他就像是说，迈克尔，你得振作起来。

699
00:30:33.100 --> 00:30:37.020
Like, basically, he's saying, you're our leader, and if you're freaking out, it's freaking
基本上，他是在说，你是我们的领导，如果你崩溃了，那大家都会

700
00:30:37.020 --> 00:30:37.640
out everyone.
跟着崩溃。

701
00:30:37.660 --> 00:30:39.880
We need to just make this a normal day.
我们得让今天变得和平常一样。

702
00:30:40.040 --> 00:30:40.840
What's on the agenda?
日程安排上有什么？

703
00:30:41.340 --> 00:30:43.600
Michael's like, well, we're supposed to have a staff meeting.
迈克尔说，好吧，我们应该开个员工会议。

704
00:30:43.900 --> 00:30:45.240
And Jim's like, great.
吉姆就说，太棒了。

705
00:30:45.400 --> 00:30:45.760
Right.
没错。

706
00:30:45.980 --> 00:30:47.420
Everyone in the conference room.
所有人到会议室来。

707
00:30:47.540 --> 00:30:50.740
Have we ever seen Jim so excited to go into the conference room before?
我们以前见过吉姆对进会议室这么兴奋吗？

708
00:30:51.440 --> 00:30:54.300
No, but he says he only slacks off when things are good.
没有，但他说了，只有在一切顺利时他才会偷懒。

709
00:30:54.300 --> 00:30:59.600
So I guess, you know, when the s**t hits the fan, he becomes very professional.
所以我猜，你知道，当麻烦找上门时，他就会变得非常专业。

710
00:30:59.860 --> 00:31:05.300
It's so funny because I feel like people would be equally freaked out by Jim suddenly having
这太搞笑了，因为我觉得大家会对吉姆突然表现出

711
00:31:05.300 --> 00:31:06.120
a work ethic.
职业道德感到同样惊慌。

712
00:31:06.460 --> 00:31:08.140
They'd be like, uh-oh, uh-oh.
他们会觉得，噢不，噢不。

713
00:31:08.340 --> 00:31:08.900
What's happening?
发生什么事了？

714
00:31:09.120 --> 00:31:10.000
Stuff is bad.
情况不妙。

715
00:31:10.160 --> 00:31:11.240
Jim wants to work.
吉姆想工作了。

716
00:31:11.420 --> 00:31:11.640
Yeah.
是啊。

717
00:31:12.180 --> 00:31:13.180
Mom is getting serious.
妈妈要认真起来了。

718
00:31:13.180 --> 00:31:14.000
What's going on?
怎么回事？

719
00:31:14.140 --> 00:31:14.620
Exactly.
没错。

720
00:31:15.200 --> 00:31:18.920
In the conference room, Jim addresses the group.
在会议室里，吉姆向大家讲话。

721
00:31:19.340 --> 00:31:22.880
At 5 minutes 56 seconds, Ryan is wearing glasses.
在5分56秒时，瑞安戴着眼镜。

722
00:31:22.880 --> 00:31:24.760
That was my big takeaway.
这是我最大的发现。

723
00:31:25.340 --> 00:31:30.100
Ryan is wearing glasses and everyone's in the conference room but Kelly.
瑞安戴着眼镜，除了凯莉，所有人都进了会议室。

724
00:31:30.700 --> 00:31:31.620
Where's Kelly?
凯莉在哪？

725
00:31:31.900 --> 00:31:32.860
Where is Kelly?
凯莉去哪了？

726
00:31:33.140 --> 00:31:33.880
Let me tell you.
我来告诉你。

727
00:31:34.200 --> 00:31:36.520
She's only in one scene this entire episode.
这一整集她只出现了一个镜头。

728
00:31:36.760 --> 00:31:37.800
What was she doing?
她在干什么？

729
00:31:38.140 --> 00:31:39.320
Where was Mindy?
敏迪去哪了？

730
00:31:39.520 --> 00:31:40.400
I don't know.
我不知道。

731
00:31:41.120 --> 00:31:44.460
Michael has to leave the conference room to take a phone call.
迈克尔不得不离开会议室去接个电话。

732
00:31:44.720 --> 00:31:47.640
And Dwight has one of my favorite lines in the episode.
德怀特说了这一集中我最喜欢的台词之一。

733
00:31:47.840 --> 00:31:48.700
What is it?
是什么？

734
00:31:48.860 --> 00:31:50.600
He says, he needs me.
他说，他需要我。

735
00:31:51.020 --> 00:31:52.200
Seat saved infinity.
座位预留到永远。

736
00:31:52.880 --> 00:31:53.240
Aw.
噢。

737
00:31:53.860 --> 00:31:55.420
Our kids save seats.
我们的孩子会占座。

738
00:31:55.620 --> 00:31:57.140
They're still in that phase of their life.
他们还处在人生的那个阶段。

739
00:31:57.240 --> 00:31:58.740
We're like, I want that seat.
我们就像是，我想要那个座位。

740
00:31:58.920 --> 00:31:59.880
That's my seat.
那是我的座位。

741
00:32:00.280 --> 00:32:01.560
Seat saved infinity.
座位预留到永远。

742
00:32:02.240 --> 00:32:03.440
Dwight came to play.
德怀特真是拼了。

743
00:32:03.740 --> 00:32:05.380
Well, Michael's going to come back.
好吧，迈克尔要回来了。

744
00:32:06.240 --> 00:32:08.440
His phone call was bad news, Angela.
他的电话是个坏消息，安吉拉。

745
00:32:08.680 --> 00:32:08.900
Yeah.
是啊。

746
00:32:09.400 --> 00:32:10.300
Very bad news.
非常坏的消息。

747
00:32:10.860 --> 00:32:13.480
There's been a murder in Savannah.
萨凡纳发生了一起谋杀案。

748
00:32:14.140 --> 00:32:16.300
And that was the end of the act break.
而那正是幕间休息的结束。

749
00:32:16.700 --> 00:32:18.080
It was supposed to be.
本该是那样的。

750
00:32:18.320 --> 00:32:20.180
They were supposed to go to commercial.
他们本该进入广告时间的。

751
00:32:20.600 --> 00:32:20.820
Yeah.
没错。

752
00:32:21.060 --> 00:32:24.260
And then when they were editing, they thought that would be stressful.
后来在剪辑的时候，他们觉得那样会让人压力很大。

753
00:32:24.640 --> 00:32:26.820
They thought it would be mean also to the audience.
他们还觉得那样对观众来说太刻薄了。

754
00:32:26.820 --> 00:32:34.640
But instead, we have this Michael talking head where we also see him going through his closet.
但取而代之的是，我们有了迈克尔的这段访谈，同时我们还能看到他在翻找自己的衣柜。

755
00:32:34.640 --> 00:32:36.080
He's looking for something.
他在找什么东西。

756
00:32:36.340 --> 00:32:37.260
His office armoire.
他的办公室衣橱。

757
00:32:37.260 --> 00:32:37.940
Yes.
没错。

758
00:32:38.240 --> 00:32:43.060
There are many games inside, and we realize there has not been a real murder.
里面有很多游戏，我们意识到并没有发生真正的谋杀案。

759
00:32:44.020 --> 00:32:46.580
But we're going to play a murder mystery game.
但我们要玩一个谋杀之谜游戏。

760
00:32:46.800 --> 00:32:47.100
Yes.
没错。

761
00:32:47.200 --> 00:32:51.020
Because Michael thinks games help distract you in stressful situations.
因为迈克尔认为游戏有助于在压力大的情况下分散注意力。

762
00:32:51.400 --> 00:32:51.760
Yes.
没错。

763
00:32:52.080 --> 00:32:53.720
Did you see the games in his armoire?
你看到他衣橱里的那些游戏了吗？

764
00:32:53.900 --> 00:32:54.400
I did.
看到了。

765
00:32:54.580 --> 00:32:55.540
Let's read them off.
我们来读一下吧。

766
00:32:55.980 --> 00:32:56.460
All right.
好的。

767
00:32:56.500 --> 00:32:58.060
I don't know if we wrote them in the same order.
我不知道我们写的顺序是不是一样。

768
00:32:58.740 --> 00:32:59.840
Well, you do one.
这样吧，你读一个。

769
00:32:59.880 --> 00:33:00.440
I'll do one.
我读一个。

770
00:33:00.540 --> 00:33:00.920
All right.
好的。

771
00:33:00.920 --> 00:33:01.720
Connect Four.
四子棋。

772
00:33:02.120 --> 00:33:02.640
Stratego.
陆战棋。

773
00:33:03.060 --> 00:33:03.580
Operation.
手术台游戏。

774
00:33:04.040 --> 00:33:04.540
Trouble.
麻烦游戏。

775
00:33:04.960 --> 00:33:05.360
Sorry.
对不起游戏。

776
00:33:05.720 --> 00:33:06.160
Risk.
风险游戏。

777
00:33:06.460 --> 00:33:06.980
Battleship.
海战棋。

778
00:33:07.660 --> 00:33:08.340
That's it.
就这些了。

779
00:33:08.440 --> 00:33:09.140
That's what I had.
我记的也是这些。

780
00:33:09.300 --> 00:33:09.820
Me too.
我也是。

781
00:33:10.200 --> 00:33:15.760
Well, the game he brings in to the conference room is called Bells, Bourbon, and Bullets,
他带到会议室的游戏叫《铃铛、波本威士忌和子弹》

782
00:33:15.840 --> 00:33:17.900
a Murder Mystery Dinner Party Game.
是一款谋杀之谜晚餐派对游戏。

783
00:33:18.180 --> 00:33:18.560
Yes.
没错。

784
00:33:18.560 --> 00:33:19.560
We got a lot of mail.
我们收到了很多邮件。

785
00:33:19.720 --> 00:33:21.560
People wanted to know, is this a real game?
大家想知道，这是真实存在的游戏吗？

786
00:33:21.700 --> 00:33:22.420
Can I buy it?
我能买到吗？

787
00:33:22.500 --> 00:33:23.240
Can I play it?
我能玩吗？

788
00:33:23.660 --> 00:33:25.380
Well, it was a made-up game.
其实，这是一个虚构的游戏。

789
00:33:25.920 --> 00:33:31.300
The box and all the cards and the props inside were created just for our episode.
盒子、所有的卡片以及里面的道具都是专门为我们这集节目制作的。

790
00:33:31.680 --> 00:33:36.900
The box and the logos were designed by our new graphic designer, Henry Sane.
盒子和标志是由我们的新平面设计师亨利·塞恩设计的。

791
00:33:37.180 --> 00:33:42.920
And Phil Shea worked with Danny Chun to come up with all of the props and paraphernalia
菲尔·谢伊和丹尼·春合作构思了所有的道具和周边物品，

792
00:33:42.920 --> 00:33:44.380
that each character would have.
每个角色都会有相应的道具。

793
00:33:44.760 --> 00:33:50.960
And Randy even shared with us that the box and cards were printed by Phil's go-to prop
兰迪甚至告诉我们，盒子和卡片是由菲尔常用的道具制造公司“手持道具室”印刷的。

794
00:33:50.960 --> 00:33:55.280
manufacturing company called The Hand Prop Room.
现在我们知道这些东西都是从哪儿来的了！

795
00:33:56.280 --> 00:33:59.180
Now we know where all this stuff comes from!
他们做得太棒了。

796
